WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.534
-Our first guest
is a world renowned chef

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.501
and Emmy-nominated TV host.

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:07.267
His new show, which is great,
"Next Level Chef,"

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:09.601
airs Wednesdays at 9:00 p.m.
on Fox.

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:12.133
Here is Gordon Ramsay,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:13.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:15.200
Thank you, bud.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.267
Welcome back to our show.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.534
-Thank you, mate.
Good to see you.

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:22.033
-It is lovely to see you.
Before we start, please,

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.901
I was just gonna ask you, 'cause
I've never done this before

00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:26.300
when we've been on the show --
please don't yell at me,

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:31.701
and -- or curse or call --
call me an idiot or anything.

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:34.234
Just this one time, Gordon.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.868
This is a time
to change things around.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:38.767
Change is good, you know?
-Change is good,

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:40.734
but sometimes, the occasional
[bleep] comes out.

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:42.033
-All right, here we go.
All right, now look.

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:44.467
-Okay.
Come on.

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:46.334
-I knew this was just gonna
go off the rails already.

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:47.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:48.467
You know what I wanted
to ask you?

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:49.467
I don't think anyone's
ever asked you.

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:50.567
'Cause I know you're married --

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:52.834
your lovely wife
and your beautiful family.

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:54.934
But when you get married
and you're -- you're an

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.868
unbelievable chef
like Gordon Ramsay is,

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:59.234
do you over-obsess
about the food?

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:01.167
What was the food
at your wedding?

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:02.634
-Oh, God,
that's a good question.

00:01:02.634 --> 00:01:05.067
This year we celebrate 25 years,
which is great. So, uh...

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:06.968
-Wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:08.434
Congratulations.
-We had something like

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:11.267
150 chefs turn out
for this wedding.

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:15.033
And we got married back in 1996
at the Café Royal.

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.734
And so I decided
to keep it really nice

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:18.434
and sort of straightforward.

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:20.734
But we did
the most amazing prawn cocktail,

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:22.901
which was a simple appetizer.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:25.667
-And for entrees,
we had this amazing ribeye

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:28.467
that was cooked on the grill
with these duck --

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:32.567
duck-fat-cooked, triple-cooked
fries with truffle.

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:34.200
And then, for dessert,
we had just finished off

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.000
with this amazing chocolate
fondant with a milk ice cream.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.767
Honestly, it was so delicious.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.267
-Yeah, see, that's good.
-But, yeah.

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:44.834
-That's simple, though --
even though it's tricky.

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:46.534
But it's kind of simple, right?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:48.234
-Yeah.
-Meat and potatoes.

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:50.534
You have ice cream
and chocolate sauce.

00:01:50.534 --> 00:01:52.200
Shrimp cocktail.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.300
"Shrimp cocktail."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.033
Wait. Can you say --
Can you say "shrimp cocktail"

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.834
in an American accent?

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:58.901
-[ Normal voice ]
Shrimp cocktail.

00:01:58.901 --> 00:02:00.234
-[ Laughing ]
That's not even close.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:01.767
Oh, my God.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:03.901
"Master Chef Jr."
is coming back.

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:05.634
-Yes.
-And I do love that show.

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:10.000
Would you be good at any
of your shows as a contestant?

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.267
-Mate, at 8 years of age,

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:16.601
I was too busy trying to kick
a soccer ball around.

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:20.901
I think, if anything, when I
came out of Paris at, what, 23,

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:23.133
getting my ass kicked
in top-flight kitchens

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:27.200
across France,
I'd probably end up

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.701
on something like
"Hell's Kitchen,"

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:32.801
that sort of high-octane,
high-pressurized boot camp...

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:35.701
-Yeah..
-...of the culinary world.

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:38.167
-Would you be good?
-I'd be [bleep] amazing.

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:39.834
[ Laughter ]
-All right -- Gordon, that --

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:41.234
You can't say that.
That's two.

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:43.133
That's two strikes.
That's two --

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:44.434
That's two strikes for you.
-It's 11:35.

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:46.367
-That's two strikes for you.
"I'm going to put you

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:47.501
on the naughty step!"

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:48.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.801
-It's 11:35.
You're allowed to cuss

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:53.501
after 9:00 in the U.K.
-No, it's actually flipped over.

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:55.200
It's already past midnight,
so now it's the morning.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:56.400
[ Laughter ]
-[Bleep]

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.667
-So it's a morning show
at this point, yeah.

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:01.734
You know, I love you on TikTok.
It makes me laugh.

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:02.934
Right? Do you guys know
what I'm talking about?

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:04.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:06.534
You do this amazing thing
on TikTok where you duet --

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.300
you watch someone make
something, and you just --

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.834
you ridicule them
and just make fun of them

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:12.534
or give them critiques.

00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:15.300
But very --
it's very good and very funny.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.934
And you're good at that.
I thought maybe

00:03:16.934 --> 00:03:20.100
if I made a sandwich,
can you critique that?

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.968
[ Laughter ]
-You, as a chef?

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:25.400
I'd love to see what --
What would you put together?

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.400
-All right, here we go.
All right.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.667
So I'm just gonna
make a sandwich

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:29.267
like I would normally
make a sandwich,

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:30.567
and you can talk.
I won't --

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:32.567
I'll try not to listen to you.
Okay?

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:33.834
-Okay.
-Okay, here we go.

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:35.834
-So...
-All right, here we go.

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:37.133
So I'm gonna
make a sandwich here.

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:40.267
I got all the spreads.
I'm gonna choose

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:43.100
this right here,
these two pieces of bread.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.234
-Plain white bread?
-And I'm going to --

00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:47.601
I don't like ham.
I don't know what that is.

00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:49.067
-Hold on, hold on.
-I don't like cheese that much

00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:52.200
unless it's melted, so --
And that bacon is ugh.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.834
So, no on that.
I'm gonna go with turkey.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.767
Oh, no.
Do I do turkey first?

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:58.033
-The butter, you donut.

00:03:58.033 --> 00:03:59.200
What about some butter
on there first?

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.934
-Do I put --
Do I put mustard or something?

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:03.901
I like mustard.
-[Bleep] me.

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:07.601
What about
some hummus or mayonnaise?

00:04:07.601 --> 00:04:08.801
How about --
-I love --

00:04:08.801 --> 00:04:10.801
Don't even say the word
mayonnaise -- gross.

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:12.667
[ Laughter ]
I love mustard.

00:04:12.667 --> 00:04:14.901
Oh, I want more turkey, right?
I can just put more.

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:17.000
I would never do mustard
in between the Turkey.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.934
Oh, my God.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:21.100
-All right, I'm gonna put onion.
Maybe onion?

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.834
-No, you don't put raw onion --
No.

00:04:23.834 --> 00:04:25.667
-I love that.
That looks good right there.

00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:28.601
I'm in, like, a --
I'm in a spicy fun mood,

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.267
like you don't know
where I'm gonna end up.

00:04:30.267 --> 00:04:32.367
So I'm gonna go a little
jalapeño on there, y'all.

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:34.400
Hello!
"Hi, y'all!

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.334
How y'all doing?!
How y'all doing?"

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:38.167
-Is that it?
-All right, let's go, bud.

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:40.601
Al right, and then maybe
I'll put some pickled jalapeños,

00:04:40.601 --> 00:04:41.968
as well, on there,
for some extra --

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:44.133
-No.
It'll turn the bread soggy.

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:47.000
-For some extra zip.
And then, if you want

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.000
to talk about zip,
put a little mustard

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.801
back on this guy.
Let's zip it up one more time!

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:52.734
-Oh, my God, no!
-And then we want

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:55.033
to crunch it down?
Crunch it down then.

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:57.367
Don't talk to me about it.
Call me later.

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:58.667
Here we go.
-It's gonna --

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:01.467
It's gonna fall apart now.
-And do you slice it?

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.400
-No, it's gonna --
Oh, my goodness.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.534
-No, I do it that way.
-It's gonna fall apart.

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:10.434
Oh, geez.
It's gonna -- oh, my gosh.

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:11.801
-Here we go.
-That was a sandwich nightmare

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:13.367
right there.
What is that thing?

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:15.934
-That is a turkey sandwich,
a la Jimmy.

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:18.234
[ Laughter ]
-A la Jimmy -- no.

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:20.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:21.801
When you lift up a sandwich
and you look at it,

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:23.868
it should look edible.
Yours looks like

00:05:23.868 --> 00:05:27.701
the inside of a [bleep] diaper.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:29.300
Look at --
-What's he talking about?

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.968
That's a --
[ Audience "Ews" ]

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:33.033
-Oh, my God.

00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:34.267
Jimmy...
-Yeah.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:35.667
-Jimmy!
-Yes!

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:37.968
Stop yelling!
I can hear you, man!

00:05:37.968 --> 00:05:40.934
-Get two slices of bread
and stick them on your ears.

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:43.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.534 --> 00:05:45.701
-Two slices of bread
and stick them on my ears?

00:05:45.701 --> 00:05:49.601
-Yes!
Quick!

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:51.868
You idiot sandwich!
What are you?!

00:05:51.868 --> 00:05:53.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:55.968
-So stupid.
Don't make me do that.

00:05:55.968 --> 00:05:58.300
-Come on.
-You called me an idiot, too.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:01.400
I told you not to do that!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.234
Whoo-hoo!

00:06:03.234 --> 00:06:05.734
Gordon Ramsay,
I love having you on.

00:06:05.734 --> 00:06:07.434
I want to talk about
"Next Level Chef."

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:08.901
I think it's genius.
I think --

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.801
How did you
think of this idea?

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:12.100
Where did it come from?

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.501
-Yeah, that's
a really good question.

00:06:13.501 --> 00:06:15.634
So, you know how tough it's been
for the restaurant business

00:06:15.634 --> 00:06:17.767
over the last two years,
so I said,

00:06:17.767 --> 00:06:19.467
"Look, let's treat this moment
as a grassroots.

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:20.834
Let's start developing
new ideas.

00:06:20.834 --> 00:06:23.067
Let's start reopening
these restaurants with new,

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:25.934
fresh ideas," and it was the
same with the production arm.

00:06:25.934 --> 00:06:28.534
So, for the first time ever, we
put together professional chefs,

00:06:28.534 --> 00:06:32.767
social-media chefs, and then
amateur chefs into one arena.

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:34.367
Stuck them
on three different levels,

00:06:34.367 --> 00:06:37.300
and then the idea was to climb
to get to the next level.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:40.467
So, this platform descends down,
you grab your ingredients,

00:06:40.467 --> 00:06:44.801
you cook ad hoc,
with a very spontaneous insight,

00:06:44.801 --> 00:06:46.934
and you create
across 45 minutes,

00:06:46.934 --> 00:06:49.067
and you cook your way
to the very top.

00:06:49.067 --> 00:06:51.367
So, yeah, super exciting.
-This is the --

00:06:51.367 --> 00:06:53.601
This is the three levels here.
The top kitchen is all, like,

00:06:53.601 --> 00:06:55.701
top-of-the-line stuff.
The middle kitchen is just

00:06:55.701 --> 00:06:57.767
a normal kitchen
you see in a restaurant.

00:06:57.767 --> 00:07:00.501
And down here is the basement,
where nothing works,

00:07:00.501 --> 00:07:02.901
the pots are all bent, and --
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.901 --> 00:07:05.968
And there's the elevator where
all the food comes down.

00:07:05.968 --> 00:07:08.334
And it is so fun to watch.

00:07:08.334 --> 00:07:10.868
And I will say,
your co-hosts are amazing.

00:07:10.868 --> 00:07:12.767
Nyesha Arrington...
-Richard and Nyesha.

00:07:12.767 --> 00:07:14.133
-...Richard Blais,
they're fantastic.

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:16.601
Nyesha, she's tough, by the way.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:07:16.601 --> 00:07:17.901
-I love that she --
-I swear to God.

00:07:17.901 --> 00:07:20.100
-I love that she threw --
threw the pan off the whole set.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:23.033
-Mate, you would last 30 seconds
in the kitchen with her.

00:07:23.033 --> 00:07:24.701
-Get a life.
Get a life.

00:07:24.701 --> 00:07:27.467
No way, man. I'd be one of
the trailblazers, man.

00:07:27.467 --> 00:07:30.100
Know what I'm talking about?
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.734
-You'd go down.
I promise you.

00:07:31.734 --> 00:07:33.667
-Yeah, right.
I love the show,

00:07:33.667 --> 00:07:36.834
and I already know who won.

00:07:36.834 --> 00:07:39.734
-What?
-Yeah, I think I know who won.

00:07:39.734 --> 00:07:41.501
I'm so good at this.
I'm so good.

00:07:41.501 --> 00:07:44.467
I watched the show.
-What, with putting

00:07:44.467 --> 00:07:45.901
a sandwich together like that
piece of [bleep]?

00:07:45.901 --> 00:07:47.167
You know who's won?
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.167 --> 00:07:50.834
Mate, you got no chance.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:50.834 --> 00:07:52.267
Here's a look
at "Next Level Chef."

00:07:52.267 --> 00:07:53.767
Check this out.

00:07:53.767 --> 00:07:55.400
-Come on.
-Some of the potatoes

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:56.467
are slightly under.

00:07:56.467 --> 00:07:58.767
It's gonna be tight
to finish this.

00:07:58.767 --> 00:08:01.968
Tell me -- pomme soufflé.
-Uh, I got one.

00:08:01.968 --> 00:08:03.634
-They're not working,
drop them, right?

00:08:03.634 --> 00:08:07.167
60 seconds.
Start dressing these plates now!

00:08:07.167 --> 00:08:09.901
-Every detail at this point
has to be perfect.

00:08:09.901 --> 00:08:16.234
This is it.
-5, 4, 3, 2, 1.

00:08:16.234 --> 00:08:18.133
And stop.
Hands in the air.

00:08:18.133 --> 00:08:21.334
Well done!
-The stress!

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:23.167
[ Laughter ]

00:08:23.167 --> 00:08:24.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:24.234 --> 00:08:25.868
-It's a great show.
Congrats, buddy.

00:08:25.868 --> 00:08:28.167
Best to the fam.
Gordon Ramsay, everybody.

00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:31.968
"Next Level Chef" airs
Wednesdays at 9:00 p.m. on Fox.

